---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Off-Leash Reliability Reactive Dogs San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Experience true freedom with off-leash reliability for reactive dogs in San Jacinto. We build rock-solid communication that doesn't rely on a piece of nylon.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Off-Leash Reliability for Reactive Dogs",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/off-leash-reliability"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/leash-reactivity-bootcamp" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Leash Reactivity Bootcamp</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Off-Leash Reliability</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Off-Leash Reliability for Reactive Dogs in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          The idea of letting a reactive dog off-leash sounds like a nightmare. You’ve likely spent years death-gripping a lead at Hiram Deville Park, bracing your core every time another dog appears.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          These "what if" fears are symptoms of a lack of reliable communication. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or hand out generic advice about off-leash work. We must evaluate your dog in person to see if they have the foundation required for true freedom without a piece of nylon.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Beyond the Physical Tether
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, I specialize in the high-level communication required to take a reactive dog off-leash safely. For 8 years, I’ve been proving that reactivity doesn't have to mean a lifetime of restriction. My balanced approach uses remote communication tools as a silent, long-distance "tap" on the shoulder.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I once took a reactive dog out to the open spaces at the base of the San Jacinto Mountains. We had spent weeks building a rock-solid recall and "stop" using "Balanced Clarity" and neutral pack targets like Rocky. The moment the owner finally dropped the leash and saw their dog run, then snap back to a recall amidst distractions, was pure joy. It wasn't gambling—it was a conversation held over 50 yards of desert.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I use high-value rewards for engagement, but I also provide fair, calibrated corrections for when a dog decides to fixate or ignore a command. Without a way to enforce the "no" at a distance, you aren't training. 
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          We practice in the open spaces near Valley-Wide Recreation and on local trails where the occasional mountain biker keeps the stakes high. My goal is a dog mentally tethered to you regardless of what’s happening on the trail. Stop living life on a short leash.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Apply for a Free Behavioral Assessment and experience true freedom.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
